(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Functions, built-in functions, cells, code objects and modules."] [8 2 "// MethodDescrType is method_descriptor (descrobject.c's PyMethodDescr_Type): a built-in type's method as its class"] [9 2 "// holds it (list.append), a *Builtin with an Owner and no Self (queue 286: multiprocessing.reduction registers its"] [10 2 "// method descriptors' reducer for type(list.append), which was builtin_function_or_method, so ForkingPickler asked"] [11 2 "// every built-in function it pickled for an __objclass__)"] [18 1 "// Function is a Python function: a code object with its globals, defaults and closure"] [19 1 "// (CPython's PyFunctionObject)."] [26 20 "// positional defaults, or nil"] [27 20 "// keyword-only defaults, or nil"] [29 20 "// __annotate__, or nil"] [30 20 "// __type_params__, or nil"] [31 20 "// __dict__, made on first use"] [34 2 "// GlobalsMap is the globals when FunctionType(code, globals) was given a dict subclass's instance (queue 205f:"] [35 2 "// annotationlib's _StringifierDict), Globals its dict: the function's global loads go through its __getitem__"] [36 2 "// (CPython's LOAD_GLOBAL on non-exact globals, PyMapping_GetOptionalItem: its __missing__), nil for a dict"] [42 1 "// Builtin is a function implemented in Go (CPython's builtin_function_or_method)."] [46 14 "// the bound object of a method, or nil"] [47 2 "// objectDescr: object's method that left object's dict through the class (methodDescrs[b] is ObjectType)"] [49 2 "// wakeup: a task's task_wakeup, a node of finalize.go's graph (a pending task's cycle runs through it)"] [51 2 "// dropsArg: a consumer that keeps no reference to its arguments once it returns (next, any, all, min, max, sum,"] [52 2 "// sorted): a generator it leaves suspended, made just before by the caller, dies at its return (queue 297)"] [54 2 "// Owner is the type a method of a built-in type's dict belongs to (d_type, m_class's); unchecked: a class or"] [55 2 "// static method, its first argument no instance of Owner"] [67 1 "// isMethodDescr: b is a method descriptor (a built-in type's method, unbound; method_descriptor)."] [70 1 "// Cell is a closure's cell; Value nil is empty (unbound)."] [75 1 "// CodeObject is a code object as a Python value (the IR's {:code ...} constants)."] [80 1 "// Module is a module: its name and namespace."] [84 2 "// Cls is a subclass of module this module is an instance of (six's _LazyModule, queue 205), nil for module itself"] [86 2 "// slots are a subclass's __slots__' values (queue 226)"] [97 1 "// builtinFuncModules are the built-in modules' functions' modules (PY6d's REQUEST: a function's __module__,"] [98 1 "// CPython's m_module, which pickle saves it by)."] [115 4 "// method_vectorcall's check: a method descriptor called with its instance first"] [124 37 "// one allocation (queue 210: append grew it a second time)"] [129 4 "// method_check_args (PY7: dict.update() was a Go panic, test_ordered_dict's"] [130 4 "// CPythonBuiltinDictTests.test_update)"] [137 2 "// meth_richcompare: the same function of the same object; meth_hash not from the object's own hash"] [157 62 "// meth_repr"] [160 41 "// meth_repr of tp_new_wrapper's builtin, bound to its type"] [165 2 "// method_descriptor (queue 286): called as a method descriptor is (BuiltinType's call slot checks the instance),"] [166 2 "// method_repr, method_get (descr_check: the instance's type, the class's own as the class is asked), descr_reduce"] [196 2 "// builtin_function_or_method's __module__ (PY6d's REQUEST): a module's function's module, a builtin's"] [197 2 "// \"builtins\", else None (pickle's whichmodule then finds the function in sys.modules)"] [198 2 "// a built-in method named like a slot (a generator's __next__) has the slot wrapper's doc (typeobject.c's slotdefs)"] [222 2 "// methodobject.c's meth_reduce (PY6d's REQUEST: pickle saves a built-in function by name): a function's"] [223 2 "// qualified name, a bound method as getattr(self, name)"] [239 3 "// CPython's \"at 0x...\", the address an identity number (asyncio's Handle reprs and their tests: PY6h's"] [240 3 "// REQUEST, queue 200)"] [249 2 "// cell([contents]): Objects/cellobject.c's cell_new, cell_repr and cell_richcompare (queue 205f: annotationlib's"] [250 2 "// _build_closure makes the stringifiers' cells)"] [271 35 "// tp_richcompare without tp_hash: hash() refuses a cell"] [281 3 "// empty cells come before anything else (cell_compare_impl)"] [307 3 "// module_repr: importlib's _module_repr once importlib is the import system (PY6b's request)"] [313 4 "// importlib's _module_repr: a module with a location is \"from\" it"] [318 2 "// module(name, doc=None), CPython's module_init; a subclass's instance (queue 205: six's _MovedItems) made empty"] [319 2 "// as new_module makes it, its __init__ (module.__init__ through super()) filling it"] [342 2 "// module_new: an uninitialized module (its dict empty), any arguments; module_init fills it"] [358 2 "// module_getsets: __annotations__ and __annotate__ (PEP 649), data descriptors before the dict"] [363 38 "// a subclass's instance: its class's data descriptors first"] [391 4 "// a subclass's instance: the generic lookup (its class's descriptors around the dict), then the"] [392 4 "// dict's __getattr__ (module_getattro)"] [407 23 "// PY6a (enum's global_enum): module_getattro's data descriptors first"] [417 5 "// 3.15 (queue 239, _Py_module_getattro_impl): a lazy import's placeholder reified in the module's dict"] [422 3 "// the type's methods (__dir__, __repr__ ...), then the module's __getattr__ (PEP 562)"] [427 4 "// a pending submodule of a lazy import (_PyImport_TryLoadLazySubmodule), then the dict again"] [443 5 "// module_get_resolved_dict_item: a lazy __getattr__ reified, unless it is resolving"] [456 2 "// module.__dir__ (module_dir, queue 223: traceback's suggestions call it): the dict's __dir__ function called,"] [457 2 "// else the dict's keys"] [477 1 "// functionNew is function(code, globals, name=None, argdefs=None, closure=None, kwdefaults=None), types.FunctionType"] [478 1 "// called: Objects/funcobject.c's func_new (its clinic's argument checks, then func_new_impl's in its order, and their"] [479 1 "// messages) over PyFunction_New (the code's name, qualname and docstring, the globals' __name__ as __module__, the"] [480 1 "// builtins from the globals' __builtins__). Queue 205f: annotationlib's FORWARDREF and STRING formats call an"] [481 1 "// __annotate__'s code with a _StringifierDict as its globals (typing.NamedTuple's annotated classes, pip's import)."] [547 2 "// _PyEval_BuiltinsFromGlobals: the globals' __builtins__ (a module its dict), else the running frame's"] [567 19 "// PyFunction_EVENT_CREATE (queue 274)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[103 58] [104 39] [119 26] [131 27] [157 34] [160 28] [177 21] [200 23] [201 32] [209 31] [212 36] [216 58] [233 34] [252 38] [255 41] [308 42] [312 47] [350 28] [394 32] [400 41] [415 39] [416 32] [423 51] [433 41] [434 34] [441 40] [442 33] [448 79] [470 30] [495 12] [495 19] [504 31] [510 34] [516 34] [524 37] [537 29] [540 12] [540 19] [548 40] [549 26] [551 31] [556 26]]} (go/file "func.go" :imports [])

